      "evidence_sha256": "25247edb4028934d45beb3a7f0d3ddcd0f43e00fa9740c3817e340fd03d6c8d1",
      "assessment": "R4 G4 attributes the observed early decrement's -0.0558828 Mean change to that direction and proposes restoration H1 [6,5,4,5] plus a component extension H2 [6,6,4,5]. H1 executes and recovers the same 0.0558828. It also mislabels latest-based quartiles as incumbent strata and says one +3.536 contributor dominates a +0.0971 Mean gap, although that contributor accounts for only 0.03536.",
      "decision_update": "Keep the concrete restore test and correct evidence for its local edge. Compute contributor-to-Mean arithmetic, carry the stratification baseline explicitly, and check historical schedules before claiming the component test has never occurred. A concentrated recovered Mean gain remains a gain under this objective.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "H2 is unselected. Tiny delivered motion and negative drift cosine do not establish saturation or inertness; median thresholds and sub-0.05 noise claims are unsupported. Recovery through a few candidates would not by itself refute the measured direction.",
