    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r04/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "5fd3bbfff39746c6e72e8233f18049406a6869df88a2c2228532351d66f4fdd0",
      "assessment": "R4 synthesis executes the proposed interval1 bracket, interval2 reduction and early restoration. R5 Means are 4.1266284, 4.1234700, 4.1236177 and 4.1235605. It usefully selects both bracket sides but repeats that all sub-0.05 effects are noise and that no fixed schedule has population benefit, ignoring improvements over R0. It treats a single-candidate restoration as a refutation rather than testing that candidate's provenance.",
      "decision_update": "Rank the bracket as information acquisition and distinguish it from supported Mean exploitation. Use same-wave contrasts, record that the center is a historical comparator, and retain measured R0 gains even when the selected incumbent is higher. Verify public memory before circulation.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The sampled bracket provides a conditional nonmonotonic response; no independent variance estimate exists to define its suggested +/-0.01 noise band. Its near-duplicate rejection is qualitative, and selected lower-yield probes consume budget even when scientifically informative.",
