      "evidence_sha256": "36ed7a1e60a339180fdde37f9b5aa643ca2be0391a3a2d44b5d981da8b0f8ea9",
      "assessment": "R5 G1 correctly reads the exhausted budget and the latest interval1 increment's -0.000136142 source change. It proposes restoration and an interval2 trim only for review. It nevertheless says no fixed schedule has Mean benefit because none beats the incumbent and introduces clipping as an alternative despite the measured zero-clipping history.",
      "decision_update": "Keep the conservative interpretation of a weak local response and the no-R6 boundary. Compare R0 gain, source-action gain and selected-incumbent deficit separately. Require current evidence before invoking clipping and do not turn a nearly zero median into a mandatory Mean-benefit gate.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Both proposals are unexecuted and cannot have measured affinity assigned. Conditional near-null response does not prove universal interval inactivity, while counterpart R5 G2 is private until synthesis and must not be assumed in this analyst's reasoning.",
